            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\n> I add `vim.opt.termguicolors = true` on `init.lua` file so that the same colorscheme works correctly when using nvim over SSH.\n\nIf that fixes things, that it is an expected behavior. The default color scheme 'miniwinter' comes from 'mini.hues' module. In turn, it [doesn't define highlighting for \"16 color\" terminals](https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-hues.html#module-notes).\n\nBy default Neovim should automatically identify if the terminal emulator supports 24-bit colors and enable them (by enabling 'termguicolors' option by default). Probably in this case when doing SSH this automatic check fails.\n\nMaybe one thing that can be improved is that 'mini.hues' can show a warning if 'termguicolors' is not enabled. I'll look into it. But even with that, this issue describes an expected behavior.",
